      "markdown": "## In plain English\n\nThe ? annotation tells the compiler that a reference may be null when nullable analysis is enabled.\n\n## Why you use it\n\nGet warnings when you might use missing data without checking it.\n\n## Small example\n\n```csharp\nstring? input = Console.ReadLine();\nif (input is not null) Console.WriteLine(input.Length);\n```\n\nExamples are small fragments; declarations may belong inside a class, and SQL/HTTP examples are shown as comments.\n\n## Common mistake\n\nstring? does not validate text or automatically prevent runtime errors. A plain string annotation is not a runtime null barrier either.\n\n## Check your understanding\n\nCan a string? variable contain ordinary nonempty text?"
