      "markdown": "## In plain English\n\nA compact anonymous function written using =>.\n\n## Why you use it\n\nSupply a small operation or condition to another method.\n\n## Small example\n\n```csharp\nint[] scores = { 40, 70, 90 };\nvar passed = scores.Where(score => score >= 50);\n```\n\nExamples are small fragments; declarations may belong inside a class, and SQL/HTTP examples are shown as comments.\n\n## Common mistake\n\nThe parameter name score represents one item at a time, not the whole collection.\n\n## Check your understanding\n\nWhat does score => score >= 50 return for one score?"
