      "kind": "glossary",
      "title": "Unit test",
      "group": "Errors & testing",
      "week": 7,
      "markdown": "## In plain English\n\nAn automated check of a small unit of behavior, commonly a method or class, isolated from slow external systems.\n\n## Why you use it\n\nProtect business rules and make changes safer.\n\n## Small example\n\n```csharp\n[Fact]\npublic void AddingTwoNumbersReturnsTheirSum()\n{\n    Assert.Equal(5, Calculations.Add(2, 3));\n}\n// Requires xUnit and your own Calculations.Add implementation.\n```\n\nExamples are small fragments; declarations may belong inside a class, and SQL/HTTP examples are shown as comments.\n\n## Common mistake\n\nA high test count is not proof of good coverage. Check meaningful boundaries and failures.\n\n## Check your understanding\n\nWhich test would catch allowing a quantity of zero?"
