      "kind": "glossary",
      "title": "Cancellation token",
      "group": "Async & resources",
      "week": 12,
      "markdown": "## In plain English\n\nA cooperative signal requesting that an operation stop.\n\n## Why you use it\n\nStop unnecessary work when a user cancels or a request ends.\n\n## Small example\n\n```csharp\nstatic Task<string> FetchAsync(HttpClient client, string url, CancellationToken token)\n    => client.GetStringAsync(url, token);\n```\n\nExamples are small fragments; declarations may belong inside a class, and SQL/HTTP examples are shown as comments.\n\n## Common mistake\n\nCancellation requests do not forcibly terminate arbitrary code. The operation must observe the token.\n\n## Check your understanding\n\nWhy should an API pass the request cancellation token to database calls?"
