      "group": "Databases",
      "week": 13,
      "markdown": "## In plain English\n\nA primary key identifies a row uniquely. A foreign key constrains a relationship to a referenced key.\n\n## Why you use it\n\nConnect orders to customers and prevent invalid references.\n\n## Small example\n\n```csharp\n// Customers: Id is the primary key.\n// Orders: CustomerId references Customers.Id.\n```\n\nExamples are small fragments; declarations may belong inside a class, and SQL/HTTP examples are shown as comments.\n\n## Common mistake\n\nA foreign key does not automatically fetch related rows, and it is not permission to view them.\n\n## Check your understanding\n\nWhat should happen if an order references a nonexistent customer?"
