      "markdown": "## In plain English\n\nA SQL operation combining rows according to a matching condition.\n\n## Why you use it\n\nRead order and customer information in one query.\n\n## Small example\n\n```csharp\n// SELECT o.Id, c.Name\n// FROM Orders o\n// INNER JOIN Customers c ON o.CustomerId = c.Id;\n```\n\nExamples are small fragments; declarations may belong inside a class, and SQL/HTTP examples are shown as comments.\n\n## Common mistake\n\nOne-to-many joins can produce several rows per parent. Check cardinality before summing totals.\n\n## Check your understanding\n\nHow does a LEFT JOIN treat a left-side row with no match?"
