      "week": 15,
      "markdown": "## In plain English\n\nA group of database operations treated as a unit that can be committed or rolled back.\n\n## Why you use it\n\nAvoid saving only part of a related change.\n\n## Small example\n\n```csharp\n// Begin transaction.\n// Insert an order and its items.\n// Commit together, or roll back if any required write fails.\n```\n\nExamples are small fragments; declarations may belong inside a class, and SQL/HTTP examples are shown as comments.\n\n## Common mistake\n\nWrapping operations in a transaction does not solve every concurrency issue; isolation and constraints matter.\n\n## Check your understanding\n\nWhy should creating an order and its required items be atomic?"
