      "markdown": "## Typography and desktop-publishing fundamentals\n\nArrange text so readers can navigate and understand it. Typography concerns the form and spacing of text; layout organizes the whole page.\n\nThis is an introductory guide inferred from your course title, not your lecturer’s syllabus or an exam checklist. Compare it with your actual lectures and assignments.\n\n## Before you start\n\nBasic text editing and document formatting.\n\n## Main points explained\n\n- Typeface and font: a typeface describes a design family; a font is a particular usable instance or resource. Ensure Polish characters such as ą, ł and ź are supported.\n- Hierarchy: consistent titles, headings, body text and captions communicate importance. Semantic heading structure matters as well as visual size.\n- Spacing: kerning adjusts specific letter pairs, tracking adjusts spacing across text, and leading or line-height controls distance between lines.\n- Readability: line length, size, contrast and alignment interact. Long paragraphs in all capitals or very tight spacing make studying harder.\n- Layout systems: margins, columns and grids create alignment. Paragraph styles help maintain consistency across a long report.\n- Digital versus print output: screen reflow, selectable text, font licensing, image resolution and print specifications require different checks. Exporting a PDF does not automatically make it accessible.\n\n## Step-by-step practice\n\n1. Format a two-page course summary with one title, semantic section headings, body text and captions.\n2. Compare two line lengths and line-heights with the same paragraph; explain which is easier to read and why.\n3. Check Polish glyphs, heading consistency and text selection in the exported document; inspect required print settings with your lecturer.\n\n## Recall questions\n\n1. Is making text bold equivalent to a semantic heading?\n2. How are kerning and tracking different?\n3. Why use paragraph styles?\n\nTry answering aloud before opening the answer guidance below. Record your explanation and evidence in your personal notes.\n\n## Answer guidance\n\n1. **Is making text bold equivalent to a semantic heading?** No. Appearance alone does not communicate document structure to assistive tools.\n2. **How are kerning and tracking different?** Kerning adjusts selected character pairs; tracking changes spacing across a span of text.\n3. **Why use paragraph styles?** A shared style makes formatting consistent and allows controlled document-wide changes.\n\n## Common mistake\n\nUsing many decorative fonts to create hierarchy. Establish a small consistent system and verify that licenses permit your use.\n\n## Further study · primary resources\n\n- [MDN · Learn web development](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn_web_development)\n- [W3C WAI · accessibility tutorials](https://www.w3.org/WAI/tutorials/)\n\nThese links are supplementary reading, not your university’s prescribed reading list. External pages need internet access and may change; use current official guidance for real legal, business or security decisions.\n\n## When to mark this guide reviewed\n\n- Explain the main ideas in your own words.\n- Complete the small exercise and record its outcome.\n- Answer the recall questions and note any uncertainty.\n- Compare with your lecturer’s syllabus to identify missing material.\n\nReview status tracks this guide only. It does not mean that you have passed or mastered the entire university subject."
