      "markdown": "# Professional prompt · university subjects and visual themes\n\nAct as a computer-science educator and a careful front-end engineer. Extend my existing offline Study App so I can study all my university subjects alongside my C#/.NET career roadmap in one place.\n\nPreserve these Polish course names, remove only stray HTML whitespace entities and accidental line breaks, and provide clear English explanations with important Polish terminology where useful:\n\n1. Podstawy programowania\n2. Podstawy sieci\n3. Podstawy systemów operacyjnych\n4. Algorytmy i struktury danych\n5. Podstawy systemów serwerowych\n6. Wstęp do bezpieczeństwa danych\n7. Zaawansowane sieci komputerowe\n8. Technologie informacyjne i ochrona własności intelektualnej\n9. Systemy operacyjne\n10. Sztuczna inteligencja\n11. Zarządzanie bezpieczeństwem informacji\n12. Podstawy typografii i składu komputerowego\n13. Internet Rzeczy\n14. Zakładanie działalności gospodarczej\n15. Analiza danych/uczenie maszynowe (ML)\n16. Aplikacje internetowe\n17. Inżynieria programowania\n18. Grafika komputerowa i komunikacja człowiek komputer\n19. Projektowanie systemów baz danych\n20. Projektowanie i utrzymanie portali internetowych\n\nFor every subject, explain what it covers, prerequisites, its main concepts and terms, a step-by-step practical exercise, common mistakes, recall questions with short answer guidance, useful primary learning resources, and relevant links to my other subjects or .NET roadmap. Keep introductory and advanced networking, operating systems, and security courses distinct. These should be introductory guides inferred from course titles, not invented university syllabi or promises about exam coverage. Use fictional data and safe local labs. Verify legal/business references with official sources; avoid prescribing registration, tax or compliance decisions.\n\nIntegrate the guides into the existing study section with an obvious course filter and shortcut. Support Polish searches with or without accents, English topic searches, personal notes, reusable study threads and reversible review tracking. Reuse the current backup system without resetting or duplicating previous progress. A reviewed guide must not be presented as passing the university course.\n\nExpand Appearance with eight additional coherent color palettes, including both dark and light choices. Change the coordinated surfaces, accents, buttons and focus states—not only one isolated color. Preserve existing themes, keep regular text and primary controls readable, save the selection across reloads, and keep the interface usable on smaller screens.\n\nImplement the changes in the existing browser app without uploading private data or changing the separate native edition. Preserve user changes, back up replaced source files, and validate content completeness, course navigation, search, notes, review persistence, backup recovery, theme persistence and contrast calculations. Report precisely what was implemented and what was tested. Use this prompt now to carry out the work rather than only returning a proposal.\n"
